@page "/car"
@attribute [Authorize]
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@inject EvInfo Vehicle
@inject ChargingLimits Limits
@inject ConfiguredVehicleFeed Feed
@inject IEvEditor Editor
@inject IVehiclePortalReader Portal
@inject IVehicleStateRefresh Refresh
@inject IVehicleTelemetry Telemetry
@inject TimeProvider Time

@*
    The car: the whole of it, on one page (issues #214, #227).

    #214 gave the car a form and put "does that account work" on a second page, /vehicle-portal, on the
    grounds that this page was "which car, and which account" and that one was "does it work". That
    reads well as a sentence and badly as a journey: the sequence #214 itself prescribes is save →
    restart → sign in → ask the car, and it crossed the navigation twice for one sitting. Neither page
    was useful without the other, and nothing on either was long enough to need a page of its own.

    So the sections are in the order the work is done: Edit → Account → Ask the car → Running → Feed →
    Diagnostics. The form at the top edits what the NEXT start reads; everything under it is what this
    process resolved at startup and is running with.

    /vehicle-portal survives as a redirect (VehiclePortalRedirect.razor) rather than a 404, because
    docs/VW_PORTAL_SETUP.md has been telling owners to go there since #137.

    The other half of #227: what an owner saw on the old page depended on the manufacturer, and no
    choice got both halves of it. The sign-in was registered only for volkswagen.de and MyŠkoda, so
    for the other three the block vanished silently; the read button was the Data Act portal's alone,
    so the other four landed on a red "not configured" and a hint telling them to set VW_* keys — which
    for a live feed would arrange a Data Act portal that #212 then sets aside. Both halves now key on
    the feed this installation actually runs, and both say something for every one of the five.
*@

<SiteTitle Page="@CarText.CarPageTitle" />

<h1>@CarText.CarTitle</h1>

<p class="muted">
    @CarText.CarIntro
</p>

<CarEditorForm />

<VehicleAccount Feed="_runningFeed" />

<h2>@CarText.AskTheCarHeading</h2>

@*
    One button, against whatever feed this installation has (#227).

    It used to be the Data Act portal's reader and nothing else, which is why four of the five choices
    met a red error. What generalises it is that IVehicleUpdateService.FetchAsync -- the call the
    polling worker makes on a clock -- is the same call made because somebody asked, which is exactly
    what IVehicleStateRefresh already is (#168).

    The two differ in one way that has to be said out loud rather than papered over: a Data Act read is
    fed to nothing, and a live feed's fetch writes to the holder like any other fetch. That is the
    better behaviour -- an owner pressing a button wants the dashboard to catch up -- but it makes one
    sentence about "what this shows is fed to nothing" false for two of the five, so each source says
    what its own press does.

    Neither one happens on a render. Opening this page must never replay a password or email anybody a
    code.
*@
@if (_runningFeed == VehicleFeed.DataAct)
{
    <p class="muted">
        @Localized.Rich(CarText.PortalIntro, @<text>@(Portal.PortalName)</text>, @<text>@(CarName)</text>, @<em>@CarText.PortalIntro_2</em>)
    </p>

    @if (!Portal.IsConfigured)
    {
        @*
            Red here and nowhere else: this is the one installation that asked for this portal, so
            something missing from it really is missing. The old hint named VW_BRAND, VW_USERNAME and
            VW_PASSWORD in .env; since #214 those are fields in the form above, which is where an owner
            who has just read this can actually go.
        *@
        <p class="error" id="portal-unconfigured">
            @Localized.Format(CarText.NotConfiguredNeeds, Localized.Say(Portal.DescribeWhatIsMissingPhrase(), Portal.DescribeWhatIsMissing()))
        </p>

        <p class="hint">
            @Localized.Rich(CarText.PortalFieldsHint, @<em>@CarText.PortalFieldsHint_0</em>, @<em>@CarText.PortalFieldsHint_1</em>, @<em>@CarText.PortalFieldsHint_2</em>, @<em>@CarText.PortalFieldsHint_3</em>, @<em>@CarText.PortalFieldsHint_4</em>, @<code>docs/VW_PORTAL_SETUP.md</code>)
        </p>
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="actions">
            <button type="button" class="secondary" id="car-ask" disabled="@_busy" @onclick="ReadPortalAsync">
                @(_busy ? CarText.AskingTheCar : CarText.AskTheCar)
            </button>
        </div>

        <p class="hint">
            @CarText.SignsInAfresh
        </p>
    }
}
else if (_runningFeed is VehicleFeed.Volkswagen or VehicleFeed.Skoda)
{
    @if (Feed.Service is { } service)
    {
        <p class="muted">
            @Localized.Rich(CarText.FeedIntro, @<text>@(service.DisplayName)</text>, @<text>@(CarName)</text>, @<em>@CarText.FeedIntro_2</em>)
        </p>

        <div class="actions">
            <button type="button" class="secondary" id="car-ask" disabled="@_busy" @onclick="AskFeedAsync">
                @(_busy ? CarText.AskingTheCar : CarText.AskTheCar)
            </button>
        </div>

        <p class="hint">
            @CarText.FeedAskHint
        </p>
    }
    else
    {
        @*
            The feed is switched on and did not start — its fields are not all filled in, so nothing
            was registered to ask. Not an error about a portal nobody chose, which is what this page
            used to show: a sentence about the feed that was chosen.
        *@
        <p class="muted" id="car-ask-unavailable">
            @CarText.NothingToAskYet
        </p>
    }
}
else if (_runningFeed == VehicleFeed.OwnTopic)
{
    <p class="muted" id="car-ask-own-topic">
        @Localized.Rich(
            CarText.OwnTopicNothingToPress,
            string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Vehicle.TelemetryTopic) ? @<text>@CarText.TheTopicInTheForm</text> : @<code>@Vehicle.TelemetryTopic</code>,
            @<em>@CarText.OwnTopicNothingToPress_Cars</em>,
            @<code>captured_at</code>, @<code>soc_percent</code>, @<code>range_km</code>, @<code>charge_state</code>, @<code>plug_state</code>)
        @if (Telemetry.GetCurrentState() is { } published)
        {
            @Localized.Format(CarText.LastArrived, Units.Percent(published.SocPercent), Age(published))
        }
        else
        {
            @CarText.NothingArrived
        }
    </p>
}
else
{
    <p class="muted" id="car-ask-charge-only">
        @CarText.NothingToAskChargeOnly
    </p>
}

@*
    A Data Act read's failure, and its card. Kept apart from the live feed's below because the two
    carry different things: the portal's reading knows the bundle it came out of and whether pressing
    again could help, and a feed's fetch knows neither.
*@
@if (_reading is { Succeeded: false } failed)
{
    <p class="error">
        <strong>@FailureKind(failed.FailureKind)</strong> — @Localized.Say(failed.MessagePhrase, failed.Message ?? string.Empty, Time.LocalTimeZone)
    </p>

    <p class="hint">
        @(failed.IsWorthRetrying
            ? CarText.WorthRetrying
            : CarText.NotWorthRetrying)
    </p>
}
else if (_reading is { Succeeded: true, State: { } state })
{
    @Card(state, _reading.TargetSocPercent)

    @*
        This press against what the feed is holding (#178).

        They are different sessions, asking at different moments, and the point of saying so out loud
        is that a small disagreement here is the expected outcome rather than evidence of a fault.
        A large or persistent one is a real finding, and the feeds page is where it gets counted
        rather than eyeballed.
    *@
    @if (Telemetry.GetCurrentState() is { } held)
    {
        <p class="muted" id="against-the-feed">
            @Localized.Format(
                CarText.CardShowing,
                Units.Percent(held.SocPercent),
                string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(held.SourceId) ? CarText.TheFeed : held.SourceId,
                Age(held),
                Difference(state, held))
        </p>
    }
    else
    {
        <p class="muted" id="against-the-feed">
            @CarText.NothingOnTheCard
        </p>
    }
}

@*
    A live feed's press. A failure here keeps whatever the holder had on screen rather than blanking
    it -- an answer now known to be old is worth more than no answer, provided its age is beside it.
*@
@if (_asked is { } answer)
{
    @if (!answer.Succeeded)
    {
        <p class="error" id="car-ask-failed">@Localized.Format(CarText.CarDidNotAnswer, Localized.Say(answer.MessagePhrase, answer.Message ?? string.Empty, Time.LocalTimeZone))</p>
    }

    @if (answer.State is { } reading)
    {
        @Card(reading, null)

        <p class="muted table-note" id="car-ask-source">
            @(answer.IsFresh
                ? Localized.Format(CarText.FreshFrom, answer.Source ?? CarText.TheFeed)
                : CarText.AlreadyHeld)
        </p>
    }
}

<h2>@CarText.Running</h2>

@if (!Vehicle.IsConfigured)
{
    <p class="muted" id="car-unconfigured">
        @CarText.NothingDescribed
    </p>
}
else
{
    <dl class="facts">
        <dt>@CarText.Name</dt>
        <dd>@Text(Vehicle.Name)</dd>

        <dt>Id</dt>
        <dd>@Text(Vehicle.Id)</dd>

        <dt>@CarText.Model</dt>
        <dd>@Text(string.Join(" ", new[] { Vehicle.Make, Vehicle.Model }.Where(part => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(part))))</dd>

        <dt>@CarText.UsableBattery</dt>
        <dd>@(Vehicle.CanTargetSoc ? Units.Capacity(Vehicle.BatteryCapacityWh) : Missing)</dd>

        <dt>@CarText.ChargeEfficiency</dt>
        <dd>@Units.Fraction(Vehicle.ChargeEfficiency)</dd>
    </dl>

    @*
        Three columns rather than one, because the interesting number is the third: what the car says,
        what the installation says, and which of them the controller is actually working to.
    *@
    <table class="grid">
        <thead>
            <tr><th>&nbsp;</th><th>@CarText.TheCarColumn</th><th>@CarText.TheInstallation</th><th>@CarText.InEffect</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>@CarText.MinimumCurrent</td>
                <td>@Units.Current(Vehicle.MinChargingCurrentAmps)</td>
                <td>@Units.Current(Limits.MinAmps == Vehicle.MinChargingCurrentAmps ? null : Limits.MinAmps)</td>
                <td>@Units.Current(Limits.MinAmps)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>@CarText.MaximumCurrent</td>
                <td>@Units.Current(Vehicle.MaxChargingCurrentAmps)</td>
                <td>@Units.Current(Limits.MaxAmps == Vehicle.MaxChargingCurrentAmps ? null : Limits.MaxAmps)</td>
                <td>@Units.Current(Limits.MaxAmps)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>@CarText.Phases</td>
                <td>@Count(Vehicle.Phases)</td>
                <td>@Count(Limits.Phases == Vehicle.Phases ? null : Limits.Phases)</td>
                <td>@Count(Limits.Phases)</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <p class="table-note muted">
        @Localized.Rich(CarText.NarrowerOfTwo, @<em>@CarText.NarrowerOfTwo_0</em>)
    </p>
}

<h2>@CarText.Feed</h2>

@*
    Which feed this process actually started, as opposed to which one the configuration asks for. They
    differ in exactly one case worth showing: the Data Act portal beside a live feed, which #212 sets
    aside with a log line nobody reads twice.
*@
@if (Feed.Service is { } running)
{
    <dl class="facts">
        <dt>@CarText.ReadingTheCar</dt>
        <dd>@running.DisplayName <span class="muted">(@running.Manufacturer)</span></dd>

        <dt>@CarText.For</dt>
        <dd>@Text(running.VehicleId)</dd>

        <dt>@CarText.State</dt>
        <dd>@Localized.Name(running.Health.State) — @Localized.Say(running.Health.Phrase, running.Health.Message, Time.LocalTimeZone)</dd>
    </dl>
}
else
{
    <p class="muted" id="no-feed">
        @CarText.NoManufacturerFeed
    </p>
}

@if (Feed.SetAside is { } setAside)
{
    <p class="table-note muted" id="feed-set-aside">@setAside</p>
}

@if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Vehicle.TelemetryTopic))
{
    <p class="table-note muted" id="own-topic">
        @Localized.Rich(CarText.OwnTopicToo, @<code>@Vehicle.TelemetryTopic</code>)
    </p>
}

<PortalDiagnostics Reading="_reading" />

@code {
    private const string Missing = Units.Missing;

    private static readonly System.Globalization.CultureInfo Invariant =
        System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture;

    /// <summary>
    /// The feed this process started, which is what the account and the button key on. Read once:
    /// nothing can change it while the page is open, because changing it is a restart.
    ///
    /// <para>The running feed rather than the saved one, deliberately. A save that has not been
    /// restarted into has changed nothing about what can be signed in to or asked; the form's own
    /// <i>Saved, not applied</i> banner is where that difference belongs.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private VehicleFeed _runningFeed;

    /// <summary>What a Data Act press came back with, or null before one.</summary>
    private VehiclePortalReading? _reading;

    /// <summary>What a live feed's press came back with, or null before one.</summary>
    private VehicleRefreshResult? _asked;

    private bool _busy;

    protected override void OnInitialized() => _runningFeed = Editor.Read().RunningFeed;

    /// <summary>The owner's word for the car, falling back to something that reads as a sentence.</summary>
    private string CarName => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Vehicle.Name) ? CarText.TheCarFallback : Vehicle.Name;

    /// <summary>
    /// The car in the dashboard card's own figures and its own component (#178).
    ///
    /// <para>Same Stat component and the same formatters as the dashboard, deliberately: the reason to
    /// look at this page beside that one is to compare them, and a difference in rounding would read
    /// as a difference in the reading. <paramref name="targetSoc"/> is the Data Act portal's — no live
    /// feed carries one — and a dash there means this source did not say.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private RenderFragment Card(VehicleState state, double? targetSoc) => @<text>
        <h3>@CarName</h3>

        <section class="stat-grid" id="car">
            <Stat Label="@CarText.CarBattery" Value="@Units.Percent(state.SocPercent)"
                  Hint="@CarText.CarBatteryPressHint" />
            <Stat Label="@CarText.CarRange" Value="@Units.Distance(state.RangeMetres)"
                  Hint="@CarText.CarRangeHint" />
            <Stat Label="@CarText.CarReadingAge" Value="@Age(state)"
                  Hint="@CarText.CarReadingAgeHint" />
            <Stat Label="@CarText.CarChargeState" Value="@Localized.Name(state.ChargeState)"
                  Hint="@CarText.CarChargeStateHint" />
            <Stat Label="@CarText.CarPlugState" Value="@Localized.Name(state.PlugState)"
                  Hint="@CarText.CarPlugStateHint" />
            <Stat Label="@CarText.TargetSoc" Value="@Units.Percent(targetSoc)"
                  Hint="@CarText.TargetSocHint" />
            <Stat Label="@CarText.TimeLeft" Value="@VehicleFormatting.ChargeTime(state)"
                  Hint="@CarText.TimeLeftHint" />
        </section>

        <p class="muted table-note">
            @Localized.Tagged(CarText.CaptureTimeNote, ("em", CarText.CaptureTimeNote_0))
        </p>
    </text>;

    /// <summary>
    /// The Data Act portal, once. Its reading is not written to the holder: that is the one thing
    /// about this source that has not changed, and the sentence above the button says so.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ReadPortalAsync()
    {
        _busy = true;
        _reading = null;
        _asked = null;
        StateHasChanged();

        try
        {
            // The reader does not throw for an expected failure -- a refused password, a consent
            // screen, a portal with nothing to give all come back as an unsuccessful reading. Only a
            // genuine bug would escape, and swallowing that here would hide it.
            _reading = await Portal.ReadAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            _busy = false;
            StateHasChanged();
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The configured live feed, once, now. The same call the worker makes, so what comes back reaches
    /// the holder and with it the dashboard — which is what an owner pressing a button is asking for.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task AskFeedAsync()
    {
        _busy = true;
        _asked = null;
        _reading = null;
        StateHasChanged();

        try
        {
            _asked = await Refresh.RefreshAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            _busy = false;
            StateHasChanged();
        }
    }

    private string Age(VehicleState state) => VehicleFormatting.Age(state, Time.GetUtcNow());

    /// <summary>
    /// How far this press and the feed's held reading are apart, as a clause to hang off the end of
    /// the sentence. Empty when there is nothing to compare — one of the two carrying no state of
    /// charge is a fact about the sources, not a disagreement between them.
    /// </summary>
    private static string Difference(VehicleState pressed, VehicleState held)
    {
        if (pressed.SocPercent is not { } here || held.SocPercent is not { } there)
        {
            return string.Empty;
        }

        // Compared at the precision both are displayed at. Two readings that print as 64% must not be
        // described as differing, whatever their third decimal places are doing.
        var gap = Math.Round(here) - Math.Round(there);

        if (gap == 0)
        {
            return " " + CarText.SameSoc;
        }

        var size = Math.Abs(gap);
        var points = (long)size;
        return " " + Localized.Format(
            gap > 0
                ? Localized.Plural(points, CarText.PointsBelow_One, CarText.PointsBelow_Few, CarText.PointsBelow_Other)
                : Localized.Plural(points, CarText.PointsAbove_One, CarText.PointsAbove_Few, CarText.PointsAbove_Other),
            points);
    }

    // The portal's failure kinds, by name; a kind this build does not name shows as it came.
    private static string? FailureKind(string? kind) =>
        kind is null ? null : CarText.ResourceManager.GetString($"PortalFailure_{kind}", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.CurrentUICulture) ?? kind;

    private static string Text(string value) => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(value) ? Missing : value;

    private static string Count(int? value) => value is { } number ? number.ToString(Invariant) : Missing;
}
